\label{lem:pg-equivalence}
Suppose \mbox{$u,v\in W$} have no common geometric zero. The following are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
\item \mbox{$K_{m-3,2}(C;L)=0$};
\item \mbox{$K_{m-2,1}(C;L)=0$};
\item $L$ is normally generated, hence very ample, and its homogeneous coordinate ring has a natural minimal free resolution.
\end{enumerate}
When these conditions hold, the resolution is pure.

\label{prop:F comp result}
    For the choices of $P_j,Q_j$ and $p$ detailed above and a suitable choice of $u,v,w$, we have:
    \begin{itemize}
    \item For $g=22,26,30$ the matrices $F_c$ have full column rank for each $c=0,\dots,m-1$.
    \item For $g=20,24,28$ the matrices $F_c$ have full column rank for each $c=1,\dots,m-1$, while $F_0$ has a two-dimensional kernel.
    \end{itemize}
